<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>
        <version>4.1.2</version>
        <relativePath/>
    </parent>

    <groupId>eu.gillstrom</groupId>
    <artifactId>railgate</artifactId>
    <version>1.7.0</version>
    <name>DORA Settlement-Layer Attestation Gate</name>
    <description>
        Settlement-rail enforcement component for DORA-compliant payment
        infrastructure. Sits at the central-bank settlement layer (RIX-INST,
        TIPS, FedNow or equivalent) and performs deterministic cryptographic
        signature verification at settlement time. Companion artefact to the
        hsm reference (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19930310) and the
        gatekeeper reference (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19930395).

        Scope:
          For each settlement request identified as a regulated payment
          (Swish utbetalning in the Swedish reference deployment, identified
          via PmtTpInf/LclInstrm or via the structural derivation
          OrgId(debtor) + PrvtId(creditor)), railgate orchestrates:

            (1) retrieval of the SHA-512 digest, RSA signature, and
                certificate serial number from the payment-network operator
                (Getswish AB in the Swedish deployment) — the digest, not
                the payload, satisfies GDPR Art 5(1)(c) data minimisation;

            (2) cryptographic verification at the supervisor's gatekeeper
                instance via POST /api/v1/verify, returning a binary
                {signatureValid, compliant} decision derived from the
                stored certificate and audit-log entry;

            (3) default-deny enforcement: settlements without a valid
                cryptographic chain to a compliant gatekeeper audit entry
                are blocked at RIX-INST level, returning a structured
                error code to the originating bank.

        Data minimisation:
          railgate never sees, transports, or stores transaction payload
          content (amounts, sender/receiver detail, business message). It
          handles cryptographic artefacts (digest, signature, cert serial,
          issuer DN), the binary verification outcome, and the settlement
          metadata listed in README.md (transaction reference, declared
          certificate serial, BICs, party-type flags, instrument code). This satisfies GDPR
          Art 5(1)(c) and the proportionality requirement implicit in
          DORA Art 32 supervisory data processing.

        Architectural role:
          The triple hsm + gatekeeper + railgate operationalises the
          quadruple-triangulation model described in the companion
          academic article. Each component answers one specific question:

            hsm        — is the key HSM-bound and on-device generated?
            gatekeeper — is the certificate-issuance compliant with
                         structural-independence requirements, and does the
                         signature verify against the stored public key?
            railgate   — is settlement permitted, given the gatekeeper
                         response and the absence of any circumvention
                         path at the settlement rail?

        Legal basis (Union law):
          DORA Regulation (EU) 2022/2554 — Articles 6.4, 6.6, 6.10, 9, 28.4(e),
            28(7), 30, 32 (oversight forum), 33(3) (assessment criteria),
            35–42 (supervisory powers).
          eIDAS Regulation (EU) 910/2014 — Articles 24–32 (qualified
            electronic signatures and signature creation devices).
          PSD2 Directive (EU) 2015/2366 — Articles 35–36 (non-discriminatory
            access to payment systems).
          GDPR Regulation (EU) 2016/679 — Article 5(1)(c) (data minimisation).

        Legal basis (Swedish national law):
          Lag (1988:1385) om Sveriges riksbank — Riksbankens uppdrag avseende
            betalningssystem (RIX-INST).
          Lag (2010:751) om betaltjänster — 8 kap. tillsyn av
            betaltjänstleverantörer.
          Förordning (2009:93) med instruktion för Finansinspektionen.

        License: MIT.
    </description>

    <developers>
        <developer>
            <id>gillstrom</id>
            <name>Niklas Gillström</name>
            <url>https://orcid.org/0009-0001-6485-4596</url>
        </developer>
    </developers>

    <licenses>
        <license>
            <name>MIT</name>
            <url>https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT</url>
            <distribution>repo</distribution>
        </license>
    </licenses>

    <properties>
        <!-- PIT worker threads; override with -Dpit.threads=N on a larger machine. -->
        <pit.threads>4</pit.threads>
        <java.version>21</java.version>
        <!-- Spring Boot 4.1.2 manages Jackson 3.1.7 and 2.21.7. These overrides move to
             3.2.4 and 2.22.4, which fix CVE-2026-110879 (GHSA-m8xf-2cr7-77ph), ahead of the parent. -->
        <jackson-bom.version>3.2.4</jackson-bom.version>
        <jackson-2-bom.version>2.22.4</jackson-2-bom.version>
        <!-- Reproducible builds: entries in the jar carry this time instead of
             the build time, so the same commit builds to the same bytes. Set
             it to the release date when cutting a release. -->
        <project.build.outputTimestamp>2026-10-31T00:00:00Z</project.build.outputTimestamp>
    </properties>

    <dependencies>
        <!-- Spring Boot -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-validation</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-security</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!-- OpenAPI / Swagger -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springdoc</groupId>
            <artifactId>springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui</artifactId>
            <version>3.2.0</version>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.webjars</groupId>
            <artifactId>swagger-ui</artifactId>
            <version>5.34.1</version>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Lombok -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.projectlombok</groupId>
            <artifactId>lombok</artifactId>
            <optional>true</optional>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Test -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-test</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                <configuration>
                    <excludes>
                        <exclude>
                            <groupId>org.projectlombok</groupId>
                            <artifactId>lombok</artifactId>
                        </exclude>
                    </excludes>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
                <configuration>
                    <annotationProcessorPaths>
                        <path>
                            <groupId>org.projectlombok</groupId>
                            <artifactId>lombok</artifactId>
                            <version>1.18.48</version>
                        </path>
                    </annotationProcessorPaths>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>

            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-enforcer-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.7.0</version>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>enforce-maven</id>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>enforce</goal>
                        </goals>
                        <configuration>
                            <rules>
                                <requireMavenVersion>
                                    <version>3.8.1</version>
                                </requireMavenVersion>
                            </rules>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>

        </plugins>
    </build>

    <profiles>
        <!--
            OWASP Dependency-Check runs only with -Powasp (mvn -Powasp verify).
            In the default build it downloaded the whole NVD database on every
            clean machine, which is slow, needs network access and failed any
            offline or sandboxed build, including one that only runs the tests.
        -->
        <profile>
            <id>owasp</id>
            <build>
                <plugins>
                    <plugin>
                        <groupId>org.owasp</groupId>
                        <artifactId>dependency-check-maven</artifactId>
                        <version>13.0.0</version>
                        <configuration>
                            <failBuildOnCVSS>7</failBuildOnCVSS>
                            <nvdApiKeyEnvironmentVariable>NVD_API_KEY</nvdApiKeyEnvironmentVariable>
                            <ossIndexPassword>${env.OSS_INDEX_TOKEN}</ossIndexPassword>
                            <formats>
                                <format>HTML</format>
                                <format>JSON</format>
                            </formats>
                            <suppressionFiles>
                                <suppressionFile>${project.basedir}/.owasp-suppressions.xml</suppressionFile>
                            </suppressionFiles>
                        </configuration>
                        <executions>
                            <execution>
                                <goals>
                                    <goal>check</goal>
                                </goals>
                            </execution>
                        </executions>
                    </plugin>
                </plugins>
            </build>
        </profile>
        <profile>
            <!--
                Mutation testing with PIT: mvn -Ppit test-compile org.pitest:pitest-maven:mutationCoverage
                Reports are written to target/pit-reports/.
            -->
            <id>pit</id>
            <build>
                <plugins>
                    <plugin>
                        <groupId>org.pitest</groupId>
                        <artifactId>pitest-maven</artifactId>
                        <version>1.30.1</version>
                        <dependencies>
                            <dependency>
                                <groupId>org.pitest</groupId>
                                <artifactId>pitest-junit5-plugin</artifactId>
                                <version>1.2.3</version>
                            </dependency>
                        </dependencies>
                        <configuration>
                            <targetClasses>
                                <param>eu.gillstrom.railgate.*</param>
                            </targetClasses>
                            <targetTests>
                                <param>eu.gillstrom.railgate.*</param>
                            </targetTests>
                            <threads>${pit.threads}</threads>
                            <!-- Every mutant is killed in 1.7.0 (497 of 497; PEER_REVIEW_GUIDE.md). -->
                            <mutationThreshold>100</mutationThreshold>
                            <timestampedReports>false</timestampedReports>
                            <outputFormats>
                                <param>HTML</param>
                                <param>CSV</param>
                            </outputFormats>
                        </configuration>
                    </plugin>
                </plugins>
            </build>
        </profile>
    </profiles>
</project>
